ariana syed who has now settled outside  of afghanistan she's an afghan pop star  and women's rights activist advocating  for the rights of women in her home  country and was on one of those  evacuation flights out of kabul in  recent days ariana joins us now from los  angeles ariana good afternoon to you  good luck to you um  what a extremely worrying and difficult  journey uh you must have had to leave  afghanistan in the last few days given  the the fraught atmosphere the chaotic  things we could see at the airport tell  us what you had to do and what it was  like to try and leave kabul  well uh i've been through a very  horrifying experience trying to leave  afghanistan and escape it was not easy  at all for me because i'm a well-known  face as you said in afghanistan and also  the fact that i've been a women's rights  activist and i've openly talked against  taliban for many many years now so i i  have been a direct target and to get out  of afghanistan in a situation like that  was not easy at all i had to go through  a few taliban checkpoints even during  the night trying to escape and get to  the airport and get to the u.s army base  uh with my fiance and uh let's put it  this way i have i think it's it's a  miracle that i was able to do that and  i'm quite grateful  but my heart goes out to all the women  and children and millions of people who  are left behind in afghanistan and they  have nowhere to go  yeah give us an idea of the desperation  outside that airport because for us here  in the uk and worldwide watching those  scenes we're not actually there but  those scenes are going to stay with us  for a long time tell us about the people  you saw there the stories you heard  every everyone with the same aim  escaping the taliban  i actually saw everything in person i  wasn't on the ground when all that was  happening  you know uh we attempted twice to go to  the airport uh because initially on the  15th of august i had a flight  unfortunately the flights couldn't take  off because the the airplane that we  were booked on was filled with with like  thousands of people in it uh with you  know people with guns inside inside the  uh airplane and unfortunately the  pilots had to run away and the plane  didn't take off the next day we  attempted to come to the airport same  story uh you know thousands of people  children crying it was a disaster it was  absolutely disastrous  and um  it's it's so unfortunate you know that  people have to go through that and  obviously you know there's one more  thing that i want to add that you know  as i said that was one of those lucky  ones with a uk passport that i was able  to get out i mean those thousands of  people who are trying to get out and  they have they cannot do that i just  feel bad for them  and you know i feel like the world has  led us down unfortunately  what are your fears for women and girls  under the new taliban regime they are  presenting a moderate face at the moment  saying that they will  preserve the rights of women and girls  they will still be able to enjoy an  education they will still be able to go  to work  you're shaking your head you don't  believe a word of it  no  i personally do not believe a word of it  i don't trust them for what we have  experienced with taliban what they did  to women in afghanistan 20 years ago  was  historic and it will stay whether it was  horror  so basically i also want to say that i  think they're portraying this space just  to be  able to be recognized by the world and  what is the guarantee that once they're  recognized they will hold on to the  world  uh  so  this this is why i think they're doing  this and i i do not believe them they  they will just turn back to uh who they  were or who do they are uh i just i just  don't believe a word i hope i mean i  hope that what they're saying they will  actually act upon it and i hope that the  world if they reach some kind of a deal  with them i hope that they will hold  them accountable for what they're saying  right now about women  arianna you talk about the horror that  women and girls faced under the taliban  that is well documented and it is a  frightening picture  for women and girls in that country to  revisit there are some girls who have  grown up not knowing the taliban and  what a shock they are going to face if  they revert back to their own ways you  say the world has let afghanistan down  what would you say to world leaders  we're about to hear from the prime  minister boris johnson we're about to  hear from the u.s president joe biden  they met with other g7 leaders today to  talk about afghanistan what do you want  to hear from them  uh three things i would like to say i  understand that they obviously cannot  take the whole country out there's like  30 something million people in  afghanistan and uh it's nice of them  that they're trying to get all the  american citizens and uk citizens out  but i want to say how can we forget  about the millions of people  who are right in afghanistan and they  have nowhere to go secondly i hope that  they can put some kind of pressure on  pakistan because we firmly believe that  all the problem in afghanistan is  because of pakistan because that's where  taliban get their trainings done that's  where they get their support and funds  from and i believe that if if the world  stop funding pakistan  maybe our problems will be less in  afghanistan and there will be less  terrorism in afghanistan i mean what was  what was the reason for the world to go  to afghanistan if we try to remember 20  years ago they went to afghanistan  saying that we are trying to get rid of  al qaeda and we're going to get rid of  taliban but 20 years later we're back in  the same spot and nothing has been done  even though there was american soldiers  lives that was lost in afghanistan uk  soldiers were  you know sacrificed in afghanistan and  after spending millions and trillions of  dollars in afghanistan nothing has been  done and they would just i cannot  believe that they would just leave us  and just go just like that overnight so  it's really shocking to me i just hope  that they can sit down together and you  know uh and and and find some kind of a  solution to bring peace in afghanistan  so that the people don't even have to  leave  ariana thank you so much for speaking to  us
 

